module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_payload_admits_a_variant_its_producer_never_makes

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data a_payload_admits_a_variant_its_producer_never_makes: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_payload_admits_a_variant_its_producer_never_makes" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "A CARRIER ADMITS A VARIANT ITS ONLY PRODUCER NEVER EMITS, so the fold over that carrier grows an arm for a state no run reaches -- and that arm is written without the care the reachable ones get, because nothing exercises it and nothing can. The invalid state is a case analysis whose unreachable arm CONTRADICTS a rule the same module states for the reachable ones, while remaining perfectly constructible by the next caller. It is not dead code: dead code is unreachable from every caller, and this is unreachable from the CURRENT ONE.",
    "THE INSTANCE, 2026-09-20, gunbc#11803: gunbc.runner_microvm_lifecycle_realize StopQuiescence carried CgroupStillHolding { readback: CgroupSubtreeReadback }, the WHOLE readback, though the only producer -- cgroup_quiescence -- routes CgroupSubtreeEmpty to CgroupQuiet and can never pair Empty with StillHolding. The fold over it answered StoppedByForce for the empty case WITHOUT consulting whether the kill was asked, while an annotation three screens above states that the outcome must never become StoppedByForce, which would claim this controller's kill did the ending, when nothing was asked. The rule and the guard disagreed, and the only thing hiding the disagreement was one caller's routing.",
    "WHY IT SURVIVED REVIEW AND EXECUTION BOTH: every claim over the type passes, because every claim supplies a value the producer could have made. The change's own witness constructed CgroupStillHolding values directly -- which is the pairing obligation working as designed -- and still could not reach the arm, because the author supplying inputs supplies the ones they are reasoning about. So the arm is simultaneously constructible, unexercised, and wrong, and no green anywhere in the corpus is weakened by it.",
    "THE REVIEW TELL, AND IT IS MECHANICAL: a case analysis with more arms than its producer has outcomes. Count the variants the constructing fold can emit; count the arms the consuming fold writes. A surplus arm is either a state the producer will emit later -- in which case say so -- or a carrier wider than the fact it carries. The second is the common one, because the wide type was already lying around and naming it cost nothing.",
    "THE REPAIR IS THE NARROWING AND NOT THE GUARD, which is the whole point of filing this separately from an ordinary wrong-arm defect. Making the unreachable arm answer correctly leaves the invalid pairing constructible and adds a check that no run executes: validation standing exactly where construction was available (DESIGN section 5). Narrowing the payload to the variants that can inhabit it DELETES the arm, so the fold has no case to answer wrongly and the invalid state loses its constructor. The repair moves the class from mitigatable to structurally impossible in one edit, and the edit is smaller than the guard.",
    "WHAT THE REPAIR CANNOT CARRY, stated because this is where the class invites a fabricated green. There is no discriminating RED for a narrowing of this kind: the old arm was unreachable in production, so a claim over it would have been permanently green, which DESIGN section 4b names as worse than absent because it is cited as coverage. What changed is REPRESENTABILITY, a compile-level fact, and exercising it needs a harness that hands invalid source to the compiler. Where no such harness exists for the subject, that MISSING HARNESS is the class's next-rung trigger rather than a permanent ceiling, and the honest evidence is the narrower type plus the existing claims over the arms that remain.",
    "THE NEIGHBOURING CLASS THIS IS NOT. gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_constant_enforces_a_law_narrower_than_its_own_annotation is a carrier too NARROW for the law its author stated -- a scalar where a relation belongs, enforcing something wider than the prose. This is the mirror: a carrier too WIDE for the fact it transports, admitting a state the world does not produce. The shared root is a carrier chosen for convenience rather than derived from what can actually inhabit it; they are kept apart because the tells differ (an annotation naming a qualifier the type cannot express, versus an arm count exceeding the producer's outcomes) and because the repairs differ (introduce the relation, versus delete the variant).",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
